-- Q2423: Professional Ethics in Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SSTS No. 1 and IRC Section 280A(c), a home office deduction requires exclusive and regular use for business. When an employer-provided office exists, the home office must also meet the convenience-of-the-employer test under Section 280A(c)(1). The CPA must evaluate these requirements before recommending the position.
Wrong (B): Working from home most of the week does not automatically qualify for the deduction. The exclusive use, regular use, and convenience-of-the-employer tests must all be met.
Wrong (C): Refusing the deduction under all circumstances is inappropriate. If the statutory requirements are satisfied, the deduction may be legitimate.
Wrong (D): A partial deduction based on days worked is not the correct standard. Section 280A(c) applies an exclusive-use test, not a proportional-use calculation.$EXPL$
