-- Q2425: Professional Ethics in Tax [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Circular 230 Section 10.34(a), by signing a return as paid preparer, the CPA represents that the return is based on all information known to the practitioner and that positions taken meet applicable standards, including at minimum a reasonable basis.
Wrong (A): Signing a return does not guarantee freedom from audit. The CPA''s representation relates to the accuracy and compliance of the positions taken, not IRS enforcement actions.
Wrong (B): The CPA is not representing personal verification of every transaction. The representation is that positions are supported by applicable standards based on known information.
Wrong (D): Signing as preparer does not create personal liability for tax deficiencies. Preparer penalties under IRC Section 6694 apply only for willful or reckless conduct.$EXPL$
