-- Q2426: Professional Ethics in Tax [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AICPA SSTS No. 7, when a CPA becomes aware of significant new developments — such as an adverse court decision — and maintains an ongoing client relationship, the CPA should consider informing the client of changed circumstances affecting previously provided written advice.
Wrong (B): While SSTS No. 7 does not impose a strict mandatory update obligation, the standard recognizes a continuing responsibility when significant developments arise during an ongoing relationship.
Wrong (C): Filing an amended return is not automatically required. The CPA''s obligation is to inform the client of the changed authority, not to unilaterally amend.
Wrong (D): Waiting for an IRS challenge fails to fulfill the CPA''s advisory role. Proactive communication about adverse developments serves the client''s interests.$EXPL$
