-- Q2427: Professional Ethics in Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AICPA SSTS No. 3, a CPA may generally rely on client-provided information but must not ignore implications of information known to the CPA. When income appears significantly understated in a cash-intensive business, the CPA must make reasonable inquiries, evaluate record reliability, and document conclusions.
Wrong (A): Accepting incomplete records without inquiry violates the CPA''s duty under SSTS No. 3. The CPA cannot ignore obvious indications of underreported income.
Wrong (B): Refusing to prepare the return and reporting the client to the IRS is not required. The CPA''s first obligation is to investigate and evaluate the records.
Wrong (D): Unilaterally adjusting income to industry averages has no basis in tax standards. The CPA must determine the correct amount through inquiry, not arbitrary adjustment.$EXPL$
