UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 6662, the accuracy-related penalty is 20% of the underpayment attributable to negligence, disregard of rules, or substantial understatement of income tax. The penalty may be avoided by showing reasonable cause and good faith under Section 6664(c).
Wrong (A): The 5% rate does not apply to accuracy-related penalties. Section 6662 imposes a flat 20% rate on the underpayment attributable to covered conduct.
Wrong (B): There is no 10% accuracy-related penalty rate. The standard rate under Section 6662 is 20%.
Wrong (D): The 75% rate applies to civil fraud under Section 6663, not negligence. The fraud penalty requires proof of intentional tax evasion by clear and convincing evidence.$EXPL$
