UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 6663, the civil fraud penalty is 75% of the underpayment attributable to fraud. The IRS must prove fraud by clear and convincing evidence. This penalty is significantly more severe than the 20% accuracy-related penalty for negligence.
Wrong (A): The 20% rate applies to the accuracy-related penalty under Section 6662 for negligence or substantial understatement, not civil fraud.
Wrong (C): There is no 50% civil fraud penalty rate in the IRC. The fraud penalty is specifically set at 75% under Section 6663.
Wrong (D): The IRC does not impose a 100% civil fraud penalty. The maximum civil fraud rate is 75% of the underpayment attributable to fraud.$EXPL$
