UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRS administrative procedures and IRC Section 7803(e), a 30-day letter gives the taxpayer the right to file a written protest and request a conference with the IRS Appeals Office. This administrative appeal provides an opportunity to resolve the dispute without litigation.
Wrong (A): The 30-day letter does not limit the taxpayer to accepting the changes. It specifically provides the right to protest and request an Appeals conference.
Wrong (B): A Tax Court petition is not available at the 30-day letter stage. Tax Court jurisdiction under IRC Section 6213(a) requires a statutory notice of deficiency (90-day letter).
Wrong (D): Ignoring the 30-day letter has consequences. The IRS will proceed to issue a statutory notice of deficiency, and the taxpayer forfeits the administrative appeal opportunity.$EXPL$
