-- Q2440: Tax Procedures [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 6662(d)(1)(A), a substantial understatement for individuals exists when the understatement exceeds the greater of $5,000 or 10% of the tax required to be shown on the return. This triggers the 20% accuracy-related penalty under Section 6662(a).
Wrong (A): The $1,000/5% threshold is incorrect. The individual substantial understatement threshold is $5,000 or 10%, not $1,000 or 5%.
Wrong (B): The $10,000/10% threshold describes the corporate standard under Section 6662(d)(1)(B), not the individual standard.
Wrong (C): The $25,000/25% threshold does not appear in Section 6662(d). The individual threshold uses $5,000 or 10% under a greater-of test.$EXPL$
